  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Tomi holds the end of a stretch for a moment, letting the question sit. Her breath steadies, and she straightens up slowly. She can feel the morning air drying the sweat on her arms — a familiar sensation, grounding.\n\n“I think I’m fine with a quick greeting.” Her voice is casual, matter-of-fact. “Something easy. Just so I know you’re around. That’s different from watching me, right?” She gives a small shrug. “I like being in my own head after a run, but I don’t need total silence every time.”\n\nShe turns a little to face him more squarely, but her posture stays relaxed, her hands at her sides. “This is good. You asking like this, I mean.” She nods once, as if confirming it to herself. “Not treating me like I need a check-in every time. I don’t.”\n\nShe lets the sentence hang just long enough to settle, then rolls her shoulders back and lets her gaze drift past him, into the yard. The stretch of grass, the fence line — ordinary morning things.\n\n“Anyway,” she says, more to the air than to him, “I’m going to finish up here. Get some water.” She bends forward into another stretch smoothly, signaling that the conversation has reached its natural end. Her focus returns to her body, to the familiar routine of cooling down.\n\nThe back steps creak slightly as she shifts her weight. The morning is quiet again, filled with the sound of birds and her own steady breathing.",
